  "investigation": {
    "at": "2026-10-19T21:59:28.073639+00:00",
    "status": "local-source-investigation",
    "facts": [
      {
        "source": "node_modules/playwright-core/lib/coreBundle.js",
        "sha256": "829521b67ed7be90c7d6d6098ff39f2241562d47e4ad7ccab13710924a56001d",
        "facts": [
          "ArtifactDispatcher.delete awaits Artifact.delete then _dispose, removing the live transport channel. Successful download.path proves browser completion.",
          "Download constructor inserts into BrowserContext._downloads; successful Artifact deletion does not remove the Download from that set.",
          "Artifact._delete awaits _localPathAfterFinished; that throws for failed/cancelled downloads. Public delete therefore cannot currently provide a successful Artifact retirement receipt for that path.",
          "Pinned-driver disposal should be checked via test-only read-only registry identity; initial claimed in-process missing-guid race was not demonstrated and is superseded by the verified Chromium burst-throttle finding."
        ]
      },
      {
        "source": "/Users/jihuayu/Documents/Codex/2026-10-15/q/work/linux-build/chromium/src/content/browser/devtools/protocol/browser_handler.cc",
        "sha256": "8fe7be266c100e544ada7f909415e49af87d99051c4d25de5f9961a69a12b961",
        "facts": [
          "Browser.cancelDownload calls DownloadItem::Cancel(true), not Remove.",
          "Download progress removes BrowserHandler observer/pending set at terminal status; that is not a DownloadManager item disposal proof.",
          "eventsEnabled belongs to the BrowserHandler session. Another session enabling/disabling events does not change the original Playwright session flag."
        ]
      },
      {
        "source": "service/docker-runtime-spec.mjs",
        "sha256": "4198849138a6f58e7879241a847c50463a92999e7a5d80355545aacb070e7a5d",
        "facts": [
          "Existing /tmp tmpfs size268435456 and cgroup2GiB are whole-session outer limits. They are not a per-download prewrite cap."
        ]
      },
      {
        "source": "/Users/jihuayu/Documents/Codex/2026-10-15/q/work/linux-build/chromium/src/components/download/internal/common/download_file_impl.cc",
        "sha256": "215d42c88b80c8ec4ec5f950cd5b7fb4dbf657a6a30f3962d38bd21c6ddb0775",
        "facts": [
          "Native write admission must cover actual append/sparse parallel paths, offsets, retries and final rename; a Node progress timer can only observe after writes."
        ]
      },
      {
        "source": "/Users/jihuayu/Documents/Codex/2026-10-15/q/work/linux-build/chromium/src/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/local_frame.cc",
        "sha256": "f314885f156e923a88eed7087b00c99aa0f55d13787aebb15398fc88fa5a9d7f",
        "facts": [
          "kBurstDownloadLimit=10; ShouldThrottleDownload silently blocks further requests until a subsequent request occurs after one second. A blocked request is not deferred and does not produce a download event.",
          "Repeated-lifecycle verifier must respect native burst policy and bound download event waits; no product limit change or same-action replay is allowed."
        ]
      }
